## New Component Development (Generators or Outputs)

This rule describes how to add a new component to Blitz, either a generator or an output, ensuring consistency across code, configuration, tests, and docs.

### Scope
- Components covered: generators (under `generator/`) and outputs (under `output/`).
- Examples: `generator/foo`, `output/bar`.

### Package and Code Structure
- Implement each new component in its own Go package:
  - Generators: `generator/<name>`
  - Outputs: `output/<name>`
- Follow the existing component API patterns:
  - Generators export `New(logger, workers, rate, ...)` and implement the generator interface.
  - Outputs export `New(logger, host, port, workers, ... )` and implement `output.Output`.
- Adhere to Uber Go Style; use camelCase struct tags and prefer `any` over `interface{}`.
- Ensure no unused imports or variables and keep code readable with meaningful names.

### Configuration
- Define configuration types and validation in `internal/config/`:
  - Add a new config struct (e.g., `FooOutputConfig` or `BarGeneratorConfig`) with `yaml` and `mapstructure` tags.
  - Add validation methods (e.g., `Validate() error`) mirroring existing patterns.
  - If the component introduces a new top-level selectable type, add an `OutputType` or `GeneratorType` value in `internal/config/output.go` or `internal/config/generator.go` respectively and include it in validation.

### Overrides (flags/env)
- Update `internal/config/override.go`:
  - Add default overrides for the new config fields using `NewOverride`.
  - If the component has TLS options, add dedicated override helpers similar to existing TCP/OTLP helpers.
  - Keep flag and env names consistent with our naming helpers (`createFlagName` and `createEnvName`).
- **CRITICAL: Update `internal/config/override_test.go` to include ALL THREE test cases:**
  - **TestOverrideDefaults**: Add the new config fields with their default values to the `expectedCfg` struct.
  - **TestOverrideFlags**: Add command-line flag arguments (e.g., `--generator-foo-workers`, `--generator-foo-rate`) AND update the `expectedCfg` struct to reflect the overridden values (not defaults).
  - **TestOverrideEnvs**: Add environment variable assignments (e.g., `BLITZ_GENERATOR_FOO_WORKERS`, `BLITZ_GENERATOR_FOO_RATE`) AND update the `expectedCfg` struct to reflect the overridden values (not defaults).
- **This is absolutely critical** - missing override tests will cause configuration overrides to fail silently in production.

### Wiring in main
- Update `cmd/blitz/main.go`:
  - Extend `switch` over `cfg.Output.Type` or `cfg.Generator.Type` to construct the new component.
  - Convert and pass any TLS config when applicable.
  - Ensure errors are handled consistently with existing branches.

### Shell Completion
- Update `cmd/blitz/completion.go`:
  - **If adding a new enum flag** (flags with specific valid values like `generator.type`, `output.type`, `logging.level`, etc.), update the `registerFlagCompletions` function:
    - Add a new `RegisterFlagCompletionFunc` call for the flag using the flag name (as created by `createFlagName` in `override.go`).
    - Provide all valid enum values as completion suggestions.
    - Use `cobra.ShellCompDirectiveNoFileComp` to prevent file completion for enum flags.
  - **Flag names**: Use the exact flag name as it appears in the flag set (e.g., `generator-type`, `output-type`, `logging-level`). These are generated by `createFlagName` which converts dots to hyphens and lowercases the result.
  - **All flags are automatically included**: Cobra's built-in completion generation automatically includes all registered flags. The `registerFlagCompletions` function only adds value suggestions for enum flags.
  - **Examples of enum flags that need completion functions**:
    - `generator-type`: generator type values (nop, json, winevt, etc.)
    - `output-type`: output type values (nop, stdout, tcp, udp, etc.)
    - `logging-type`: logging type values (stdout, file)
    - `logging-level`: log level values (debug, info, warn, error)
    - `generator-json-type`: JSON generator type values (default, pii)
    - `output-syslog-transport`: syslog transport values (tcp, udp)
    - `output-syslog-rfc`: syslog RFC values (3164, 5424)
    - TLS min version flags: TLS version values (1.2, 1.3)

### Documentation
- Create component documentation file:
  - **Generators**: Create `docs/generator/<component-name>.md`
  - **Outputs**: Create `docs/output/<component-name>.md`
  - Each component doc must include:
    - **Description**: Purpose of the component
    - **Example Logs** (for generators): Show example log output produced by the component
    - **Data Mutation** (for outputs): Explain how the output transforms data (if at all)
    - **Configuration Table**: Complete table with YAML path, flag name, environment variable, default, and description for all configuration options
    - **Example Configuration**: At least one YAML configuration example
  - Follow the format of existing component docs (e.g., `docs/generator/json.md`, `docs/output/tcp.md`)
  - Component docs are automatically included in man pages via `gen-man.sh`
- Update `README.md`:
  - Add the new component to the Components section with a brief, high-level description.
  - Place generators under "Generators" and outputs under "Outputs".
  - Keep descriptions concise (one sentence) and focused on what the component does.
  - **REQUIRED: Link to the component documentation using full GitHub URL format**: `https://github.com/observiq/blitz/blob/main/docs/generator/<name>.md` or `https://github.com/observiq/blitz/blob/main/docs/output/<name>.md`
  - All component entries in the README Components section MUST include links to their documentation files using this full GitHub URL format.
- Update `docs/configuration.md`:
  - Add the new component to the valid values list for `output.type` or `generator.type`.
  - Add a link to the component documentation in the list of component links (do NOT include detailed configuration tables in the main config doc).
  - Update validation rules if new constraints are introduced.
  - Keep only global configuration in the main config doc; component-specific details belong in component docs.
  - **Update the table of contents (TOC)** if any new sections, subsections, or example configurations are added.
 - Update `docs/metrics.md`:
   - Document any new metrics emitted by the component (names, types, descriptions, labels).
   - Ensure naming follows the existing `blitz.<component>.<metric>` pattern and labels remain consistent.

### Testing
- Add unit tests in the new package as appropriate.
- Update `internal/config/override_test.go` as described above.
- If existing tests rely on exhaustive type lists, update them accordingly.
- All tests must pass after changes.
- Before opening a PR, run locally:
  - `make test` (unit tests)
  - `make lint` (linters and formatting checks)
  - `make security` (static security checks)
  All three must succeed.

### Metrics (if applicable)
- Use OpenTelemetry metrics following existing naming patterns (e.g., `blitz.<component>.<metric>`).
- Avoid duplicating transport-level metrics if wrapping an existing transport; prefer wrapper-specific metrics.

### Acceptance Checklist
- [ ] New package added under `generator/` or `output/` with clear APIs.
- [ ] Config struct and validation added to `internal/config/`.
- [ ] Overrides added to `internal/config/override.go` (flags/env), with sensible defaults.
- [ ] Tests updated in `internal/config/override_test.go` (defaults, flags, envs).
- [ ] `cmd/blitz/main.go` wiring updated to construct and use the new component.
- [ ] **Shell completion updated**: If new enum flags were added, `cmd/blitz/completion.go` `registerFlagCompletions` function updated with completion functions for those flags.
- [ ] Component documentation file created in `docs/generator/<name>.md` or `docs/output/<name>.md` with:
  - [ ] Description of component purpose
  - [ ] Example logs (generators) or data mutation explanation (outputs)
  - [ ] Complete configuration table
  - [ ] Example YAML configuration
- [ ] `README.md` Components section updated with the new component, brief description, and link to component doc.
- [ ] `docs/configuration.md` updated with component link (not detailed config tables).
- [ ] Table of contents in `docs/configuration.md` updated if new sections or examples were added.
- [ ] `docs/metrics.md` updated with any new metrics (if applicable).
- [ ] `make man` generates man page successfully with component docs included.
- [ ] Lints pass, no unused code, idiomatic Go per Uber style.
- [ ] `make test` passes locally.
- [ ] `make lint` passes locally.
- [ ] `make security` passes locally.
